Error End Event ->
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-> The Error End Event in SAP Cloud Platform Integration (SAP CPI) is used to terminate message
   processing when an error occurs. It ensures that the message is marked as failed in the
   monitoring logs, allowing for better tracking and troubleshooting.

 -> This is the component that allows you to throw an exception when an integration process ends.
    You can use this component to indicate an error condition or a failure of a process
 -> Using an Error End Event to throw the exception to default exception handlers or put the message
    back into the queue for retrying.
-> In SAP Cloud Integration (CPI), an Error End Event signals that an error has occurred during message
   processing and should be handled, typically by an exception subprocess. It causes the message to be
   marked as "Failed" in the message processing log. Unlike an Escalation End Event, which also indicates
   an issue but allows processing to continue, an Error End Event stops the main process and throws the
   exception to the exception handler




   Use Case of Error End Event
   - Exception Handling: If an integration flow encounters an error (e.g., invalid data, failed API call),
   the Error End Event stops further processing.
   - Logging & Monitoring: The failed message is logged in SAP CPI Message Processing Monitor, making
   it easier to analyze issues.
   - Controlled Failure: Instead of allowing the message to continue with incorrect data, the Error
    End Event ensures that the process stops immediately.

   Example Scenario
   Imagine an integration flow that fetches customer data from an external API. If the API call fails
    due to authentication issues, the Error End Event can be triggered to:
   - Stop message processing.
   - Log the error for further investigation.
   - Send an alert to notify administrators.


